#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/scripts

# Forum over HTTP. Runs in its own scope with its own Root; @forum arrives as a
# binding, so this script knows only that the target has Request and Filter --
# the same traits chess_web.etcs relies on, nothing forum-specific.

NetworkProvider
HttpServer web
spawn web
SetPort 8080

# SHARED WITH chess_web.etcs BY NAME, deliberately. spawn_entity retargets a
# pending name already bound to a live entity of the same module and tag, and
# PersistentNames is process-scope rather than per-script -- so whichever of the
# two scripts runs second finds THIS HttpServer instead of minting a second one
# and failing to bind 8080. Start is guarded: the second call logs "already
# started" and returns false, which is the intended outcome, not an error.
#
# Both scripts must therefore agree on the name and the port. Renaming `web`
# here, or giving it a different port, gets you two servers and a bind failure.

web.add(FileHtmlPage tree)
LoadFromDisk ./www
ListPaths tree
context NetworkProvider::HttpServer web

# One route, checked before the pages. The forum owns both halves of the
# decision: Filter answers "is this path mine", Request answers "what was
# asked for".
#
#   GET /forum/index                    thread list
#   GET /forum/selves                   participants
#   GET /forum/verify                   recompute every hash and report
#   GET /forum/alice/new/Hello          open a thread, returns its key
#   GET /forum/alice/t1/post/hi%20all   post to it
#   GET /forum/alice/t1/read            read from the top
#   GET /forum/alice/t1/read/240        resume at a cursor
#
# Every read answers with a cursor header (@. / @+N / @~N) and a bounded window,
# because a route reply is one Buffer. www/forum.html speaks that protocol.
Index node
Verify node
AddRoute @forum Request @forum Filter

Start
IsStarted

# http://localhost:8080/forum.html
